# Crafting storyline (Crafting 2.0 WP8b, AutonomousBotStorylines + CraftingDrama): a price war between two crafter gamebots
# of the same order in the same realm. The server casts roles A and B only from two real crafters that share an order
# (bot_crafting_social and bot_crafters on), and fills {recipe} with their real craft and {title} with A's real crafting
# title at the time of the episode. Four episodes, hours apart, played in /faction like the other storylines; a player
# who backs one of them in /faction gets the ending _4a (A) or _4b (B), and {player} is that player. No line names a price,
# a piece in stock or a sale: the drama is talk, the numbers stay in the trade channel where they are true. New writing.

@kind debate
@realm *

# ==== pricewar: two crafters of one order undercut each other until the realm takes notice ==========================

@topic story_pricewar
@levels 5-50
@scene story_pricewar_1
@role A type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role B type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
@role E type=Socialite
@role F type=*
A: ok who keeps undercutting my work at the broker. every time i post, someone posts lower an hour later | someone keeps posting right under my prices at the broker. every single time
B: free market {name_a}. people like a better price | thats called competition {name_a}. look it up
A: {name_b}. of course it was you | i should have known it was {name_b}
C: crafter fight in faction, grabbing a snack | ooh, crafter drama
B: im just selling my work. not my fault mine moves faster | my stuff sells. yours sits. thats not on me
A: yours moves because youre selling at cost. thats not a business, thats charity | youre barely covering the materials {name_b}. thats not selling, thats giving it away
D: wait, so gear is getting cheaper? sounds great for the rest of us | cheaper gear for everyone? keep fighting
B: my work is as good as any {title}s and priced fair. {name_a} just doesnt like it | some of us price fair. {name_a} prices like a city merchant
A: im the {title} here, {name_b}. go make some more practice pieces | im {title}. youre still doing practice pieces
E: {name_a} and {name_b} were friends last week i swear | werent you two grouping like yesterday
B: we were. then {name_a} told half the realm my work was shoddy | until {name_a} told everyone my work falls apart
A: it IS shoddy | i stand by it
F: this is the best thing in faction all week | someone write this down
B: fine. next time you post, i go lower again | watch the broker tomorrow {name_a}
A: bring it | go ahead, see who runs out of coin first

@topic story_pricewar
@levels 5-50
@scene story_pricewar_2
@role A type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role B type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=Leveler
@role E type=*
@role F type=*
A: so {name_b} is buying up the materials now. merchant was out of everything i needed | the merchant was cleaned out this morning. guess who bought it all
B: i needed materials. so did you, i guess. early bird | i got there first {name_a}. shop opens to everyone
C: round two lol | the {recipe} war continues
A: you bought three times what you need just so i couldnt work | nobody needs that many materials, {name_b}. you did it on purpose
B: im making a lot. people keep asking me instead of you | i have orders. lots of them. from your old customers
D: i just want gear that isnt held together with string, whoever makes it | can one of you just make me something decent please
A: ill make you one {name_b} cant | send me a tell, ill do it right
B: ill make it better and sooner | ill have it done before {name_a} even starts
E: this is how prices crash, by the way. two crafters and a grudge | two crafters fighting is great for the rest of us honestly
A: you know what {name_b}, the realm can decide. whose work is better | let the realm pick, {name_b}. who makes the better piece
B: fine by me. anyone whos worn both, speak up | deal. people, whose work do you wear
F: im wearing a {name_a} piece and a {name_b} piece. they both look the same to me lol | honestly i cant tell the difference
A: thats because youre not a crafter | to the untrained eye, maybe
B: thats because there IS no difference, {name_a} just charges more | see? same work. one of us just costs more

@topic story_pricewar
@levels 5-50
@scene story_pricewar_3
@role A type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role B type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
@role E type=Socialite
@role F type=*
B: {name_a} is telling people i use cheap materials now. real mature | heard {name_a} is going around saying my work falls apart
A: i said your prices are too low to be using the good stuff. thats just math | i said nothing about your materials. i said your prices dont add up
C: theyre still at it lol | day three of the {recipe} war
B: same materials as you, same merchant. ask anyone | we buy from the same merchant {name_a}. same materials, same everything
D: so the only difference is the price and the attitude | sounds like the same work with a different price tag
A: the difference is a {title} made it | the difference is who made it, and thats me
E: ok but can you two just say sorry and split the customers | honestly the realm has enough people for both of you
B: ill split when {name_a} stops trash talking my work | when {name_a} admits my work is fine, sure
A: when {name_b} stops selling at a loss to steal mine | when {name_b} stops working for free, sure
F: so never then | see you all tomorrow for round four

@topic story_pricewar
@levels 5-50
@scene story_pricewar_4
@role A type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role B type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer
@role F type=*
A: ok {name_b}. we both lost money this week. i checked | i did the math {name_b}. we both worked at a loss all week
B: ...yeah. me too. my purse is a joke right now | yeah. i noticed. im broke
C: the crafter war ends in mutual poverty, who saw that coming | everyone saw this coming
A: the only people who won are the merchants selling us materials | the material merchants are the only winners here
B: so. truce? we price fair, nobody undercuts | truce. fair prices, no more sniping at the broker
D: aww | the realm loses its cheap gear, but ok
A: truce. and your work is fine. mostly | truce. your work is fine, i was mad
B: and youre a real {title}. i was just sore about it | your work is good {name_a}, i just hated losing customers
E: back to normal prices then. so long, bargain week | the great {recipe} sale is over, folks
F: until one of them hits the next title and it starts again | see you in the next round

@topic story_pricewar
@levels 5-50
@scene story_pricewar_4a
@role A type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role B type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
@role E type=*
@role F type=Socialite
A: {name_b}, give it up. {player} picked my work and told the whole realm | {player} backed me, {name_b}. everyone saw it
B: one customer. big deal | {player} is one person {name_a}
A: one customer who talks. my orders doubled after that | the best kind of customer. and they talk
C: {player} started a run on {name_a} lol | everyone wants a {name_a} piece now
B: fine. you win this one. im going back to fair prices, i cant afford the war anymore | ok, ok. im done undercutting. my purse cant take it
A: and youre welcome to ask me for tips. {title} to you | ill even show you a trick or two {name_b}
B: dont push it {name_a} | careful {name_a}
D: {player} ended a crafter war, put that on the herald | peace in our time, thanks to {player}
E: so is {name_b} still undercutting or not | wait, does this mean prices go back up
F: {name_a}, make {player} something nice, they earned it | {player} deserves a discount for this
A: {player} has one, for life | already on it. {player} pays materials from now on

@topic story_pricewar
@levels 5-50
@scene story_pricewar_4b
@role A type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role B type=Crafter levels=5-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
@role E type=*
@role F type=Socialite
B: {name_a}, {player} went with me. said my work is just as good and fairer priced | {player} picked me, {name_a}. fair price, same quality
A: {player} just doesnt know good {recipe} | with respect, {player} doesnt know {recipe}
C: ooh {name_a} is being a sore {title} | {name_a} losing gracefully as always
B: {player} knows a fair price. so does the rest of the realm now | the realm is with me and {player}
A: fine. fine. ill drop my prices. happy? | ok. ill price fair. you win {name_b}
D: cheap gear for everyone, thanks {player} | {player} for realm treasurer
E: {name_a} coming down in price, never thought id see it | {name_a} lowering prices, the world is ending
B: and {name_a}, your work is good. i never said it wasnt. just priced like a castle | your work is fine, {name_a}. it was the price
A: ...ty. truce then | truce. dont tell anyone i said ty
F: {player} ended a crafter war, someone tell the herald | crafter peace, sponsored by {player}
